implementationPlan.description:
Modify `enqueueWSEvent()` to check `s.eventsStopped.Load()` before the select/send. If stopped, return early without sending. The full method becomes:
```go
func (s *server) enqueueWSEvent(data []byte, tenant string, jobID string) {
    if s == nil || len(data) == 0 || s.eventsStopped.Load() {
        return
    }
    select {
    case s.eventsCh <- wsEvent{data: data, tenant: strings.TrimSpace(tenant), jobID: strings.TrimSpace(jobID)}:
    default:
    }
}
```
Note: There is still a theoretical TOCTOU window between the Load() check and the send, but since the atomic store happens before close() in stopBusTaps, and the select has a default case, we also add a recover() guard as a safety net.

Add a deferred `recover()` inside `enqueueWSEvent` as a defense-in-depth measure for the TOCTOU edge case:
```go
func (s *server) enqueueWSEvent(data []byte, tenant string, jobID string) {
    if s == nil || len(data) == 0 || s.eventsStopped.Load() {
        return
    }
    defer func() {
        if r := recover(); r != nil {
            // channel was closed between check and send; safe to ignore
        }
    }()
    select {
    case s.eventsCh <- wsEvent{...}:
    default:
    }
}
```
